From e4066bb733acbb331f8c7eee024bc2bf6a20f6c5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: F4 Animation Plan <dev@f4.local>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 02:21:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/6] f4-models: grouped (hierarchy-preserving) geometry
 extraction
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Adds extract_geometry_grouped() / ModelDatabase::
extract_model_geometry_grouped(): the walk records, per output mesh,
its chain of tagged ancestors (DOF/trans/scale/switch nodes) with the
full frame + value-processing parameters, and keeps vertices in the
deepest ancestor's local space instead of baking world transforms.

- Switch values are bitmasks in FreeFalcon (BSwitchNode::Draw walks
  children with mask >>= 1); grouped mode walks EVERY child branch and
  records sw_child = bit index so the runtime can apply the same mask.
- Chain-scoped (texture, kind) merge mirrors the flat extractor's
  rule; std::map keys keep group order deterministic.
- Flat extraction path is untouched — same walk, same defaults.

Tests on the real F-16 fixture: triangle/vertex parity with the flat
path, expected DOF set {2,3,9,10} and switch set {0,1,2,3,6}, vapor
switch 6 = 2 instances x 4 children, orthonormal DOF frames, static
(empty-chain) group present, determinism.
