From 3ae733c90039f0fe171f2ff2b393ac0ae07e75a2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: F4 Animation Plan <dev@f4.local>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 02:49:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/6] f4-import: family vocab tables + animated hierarchy
 emission
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

M1 of AIRCRAFT_ANIMATION_PLAN.md — the converter half of the tag
scheme. The hard-coded FreeFalcon list is now represented exactly
once, as data:

- vocab/family/{complex,simple,heli,airdef}.json: FreeFalcon
  dof/switch index -> (§6 tag id, f4-anim channel) for all four model
  families, transcribed from dofsnswitches.h. Unmapped indices
  (COMP_FREE1..3, cockpit 100+) stay unknown.N by design.
- vocab.cpp: table loader (f4-json Reader) + guess_family() classifier
  (advisory — a wrong guess degrades to unknown.N, never wrong
  geometry).
- gltf_emitter: emit_model_hierarchy() behind
  GltfEmitOptions::emit_hierarchy (default false — the flat path and
  existing Data/ exports stay byte-compatible). Grouped extraction
  feeds a node-plan trie: root -> lod:N -> dof/sw node chains ->
  part meshes. DOF frames serialize as B-conjugated quaternions with
  the falcon local-X rotation axis mapped to glTF -Z; translators and
  scale nodes carry their vectors in extras; switch branches carry
  child + reversed per the BSwitchNode::Draw bitmask rule.
- Shared append_mesh_accessors() between flat and hierarchy paths so
  vertex baking cannot diverge.
- f4import CLI: --hierarchy and --vocab flags; family classification
  logged per model.

7 end-to-end tests: family-bound round trip through the runtime glTF
loader + anim map (flap.l/lef.r channels, vapor switch 4 branches,
pivot translation in meters, unit quaternion, rot axis -Z), triangle
parity with the flat path, unknown/unbound behavior without a table,
vocab coverage of the gear stacks, family classification of the
fixture F-16.
