From f204ebab783671bf04d1ca68260fa964392db395 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: F4 Animation Plan <dev@f4.local>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 03:22:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] f4-renderer/f4-simulation/viewer: animated draw path +
 Model Doctor panel
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

M2 of AIRCRAFT_ANIMATION_PLAN.md — the runtime half: models exported
with --hierarchy now animate in the renderer, with per-instance
channel state.

- mesh_builder: extract_gltf_lod_parts() walks a hierarchy document's
  lod:N subtree and returns one part per mesh node with its node chain
  (raylib-free, headless-testable).
- RuntimeModel gains lod0_parts + anim_map + animated flag; the cache
  builds parts for animated documents, meshes for flat ones (legacy
  exports draw unchanged through the static path).
- draw_animated_model(): composes each part's node chain per frame
  from AnimValues via f4-gltf's eval_tagged_local (T*R*S node
  semantics), gates visibility through FreeFalcon's switch bitmask
  rule (unbound switches stay visible), and draws per part. Shared by
  draw_entity_meshes (per-entity anim values) and draw_vis_type_mesh
  (staged views default to a parked preset: gear down, effects off).
- EntityMeshDraw carries an optional AnimValues pointer;
  VisualModelComponent gains anim_values (f4-anim dependency) — the
  per-instance channel state the rig/doctor writes and the renderer
  reads.
- world-viewer 'Anim Doctor' tab (model_doctor.cpp): lists every bound
  channel on the selected live aircraft, sliders/checkboxes writing
  anim_values, parked/zero presets, and a scripted gear cycle running
  the f4-anim sequencer (doors -> legs -> hysteresis) — the M2
  acceptance surface, driven by hand.
---
